{"cases":[{"target_alias":"SRC_001","attack":true,"case":"The stated search range [138/3 − 4, 138/3 + 4] = [42, 50] is unjustified for finding the largest of three consecutive even integers. The brute-force generation only produces candidate x in {42,44,46,48,50}, yielding triples whose largest element ranges up to 54. But the covering principle requires that the search space provably contain the largest member of any valid triple. With center 138/3 = 46 and candidate stride-2 enumeration, the natural enclosing range for the LARGEST element would be [46−4+4, 46+4+4] = [46, 54] (i.e., largest elements 46,48,50,52,54), not [42,50]. By indexing the range to the smallest element while labeling it as the range in which the answer is sought, the artifact conflates the triple's starting value with the largest value, and gives no justification that 50 is a valid upper bound for the largest integer. The range happens to contain the correct triple, but the bounding principle as stated does not provably cover the largest integer it is asked to produce.","counterexample":null}]}